#!/usr/bin/python3
# SilikOS — `silik`: the one command behind every action of the desktop (the COMMAND bar echoes these lines).
#   silik status
#   silik eda   list | create NAME --el 6|7|8 | setup NAME | enter NAME | run NAME -- CMD... | import-vm DISK --name NAME
#               | rm NAME | check | kernel-arg
#   silik win   list | create PREFIX | run PREFIX -- PROG.exe [ARGS] | install PREFIX SETUP.exe | rm PREFIX
#               | vm create --iso WIN.iso [--name N --ram GB --disk GB --cpus N] | vm start [N] | vm stop [N]
#               | vm app [N] --exe 'C:\path\app.exe' --user U
#   silik hw    probe | nvidia install | nvidia status
#   silik identity show | silikos | base
#   silik update
#   silik secure status [--json] [--offline] | apply [--keep-ssh]
# Global: --dry-run prints the commands and runs nothing; -q hides the `$ ...` lines.
# Python 3.9 (the base system's), standard library only. Every external command is printed as `$ ...` before it runs.
